    {
      "what": "contrast voltage",
      "pins": ["V0"],
      "why": "V0 sets LCD viewing contrast on the real glass. The module's contrast trimmer loads VCC and GND and turns in 3D, while the simulated glass draws at fixed readable contrast.",
    },
    {
      "what": "blue transmissive visibility",
      "why": "On a blue negative transmissive 1602 LCD, characters are only visible when both the display and the backlight are on. `text` returns two 16-space blank lines when either is off.",
    },
    {
      "what": "8-bit bus use and 5x10 font",
      "why": "Only D4 to D7 are wired on a PCF8574 backpack. Any non-Function-Set operation in 8-bit mode warns `chip.protocol` rule `bus_width` and is dropped. Requesting the 5x10 font (`F = 1`) warns rule `font` and keeps the 5x8 font.",
    },
  ],
